menu "T-Dongle memory diagnostics"
    config TDONGLE_MEMORY_DIAGNOSTICS
        bool "Memory diagnostics build (owner-tagged heap, per-phase capture, serial memory/members commands)"
        default n
        help
            Evidence build for the multi-tailnet memory work. Adds an owner-tagged
            allocation ledger (microlink sites plus mbedTLS), a per-membership heap
            capture at each join phase, an admission record and the serial
            "memory" / "members" commands. Costs about 2 KB of static RAM and a
            few instructions per tagged allocation. Leave off for release images:
            every hook compiles to the plain allocator call when this is off.

    config TDONGLE_MEMORY_GUARD_FLOOR_BYTES
        int "Free-heap floor enforced on tagged allocations and task creation (bytes)"
        depends on TDONGLE_MEMORY_DIAGNOSTICS
        range 0 65536
        default 12288
        help
            A tagged allocation that would leave less internal heap than this is
            refused (counted as denied) and a membership task whose stack would
            do the same is not created. This turns an out-of-memory crash during
            an over-budget membership into an ordinary start failure. Adjustable
            at run time with "memory guard <bytes>".

    config TDONGLE_MEMORY_ADMISSION_OVERRIDE
        bool "Start memberships past member_start_budget() (diagnostics only)"
        depends on TDONGLE_MEMORY_DIAGNOSTICS
        default y
        help
            Replaces the 107 KB budget and 24,000 B largest-block gate with the
            guard floor above, so a second membership can be attempted and its
            cost measured. Failed attempts are retried at most once a minute and
            every attempt is recorded by the "members" command.

    config TDONGLE_QUEUE_DEPTH_SWEEP
        int "Relay queue depth override for the throughput sweep (0 keeps 8/8/8/4)"
        depends on TDONGLE_MEMORY_DIAGNOSTICS
        range 0 8
        default 0
        help
            Sets the per-membership DERP TX, DISCO RX and WG RX queue depths to this
            value and the STUN RX depth to the smaller of this value and 4. Build
            one image per depth (1, 2, 4, 8) for the queue-depth sweep (issue #10).
endmenu
